  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Thelephantin K and CX-1 through a series of target interactions. Thelephantin K is identified as a target of SNU-387, which in turn is a target of CX-1 in multiple pathways. Additionally, SNU-387 is also a target of another compound, 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one, which also targets CX-1. Furthermore, Thelephantin K is linked to Isoamyl isobutyrate, which also targets CX-1. These findings collectively indicate that Thelephantin K may influence CX-1 through a chain of molecular interactions involving SNU-387 and other compounds. The strength of the relationship is supported by multiple pathways, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The evidence suggests a possible role for Thelephantin K in modulating CX-1 activity, but further experimental validation is required to confirm this relationship.",
